description "Sigstore signature verification for the image's own updates"

supports "fedora"

// Verifying an update is a separate decision from fetching one on a
// timer, which is why this is not part of `core/auto-updates` any more.
// An image can verify signatures without auto-updating: a manual `bootc
// upgrade` consults the same policy. The reverse is the dangerous
// configuration, so auto-updates requires this rather than the other way
// round.
provides "signature-policy"

// The cosign public key the policy names as its `keyPath`. A contract
// file because the two have to ship together: an image carrying the
// policy without the key rejects every update it is offered, and would do
// so silently until the first upgrade.
//
// It used to be a COPY in the Containerfile skeleton, beside a comment
// noting that its registries config and policy merge already lived in a
// module. This is the rest of that move.
provides-file "/etc/pki/containers/cosign.pub"
